---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Start here" description="New to GravelBoost? Learn how to pick a route, what the adventure levels mean and how to read a journey page." path="/start-here/" crumbs={[{ name: 'Start here', href: '/start-here/' }]}>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="narrow prose">
      <h1>Start here</h1>
      <p>GravelBoost helps you find adventure rides in Europe that are not extreme. Every route is ridden first, so we can tell you what it is really like.</p>
      <h2>Pick a route in three steps</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Choose a <a href="/destinations/">destination</a>.</li>
        <li>Check the first screen of a journey: distance, climbing, time, surface and adventure level.</li>
        <li>Read the <strong>Honest answers</strong>, then get the pack with the GPX and the offline guide.</li>
      </ol>
      <h2>Adventure level</h2>
      <p>Every journey has a level from 1 to 5.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>1</strong>: Easy. Wide, firm paths and short days.</li>
        <li><strong>2</strong>: Accessible. Mostly firm gravel, a few soft parts.</li>
        <li><strong>3</strong>: Adventurous. Longer days, sand or rough bits.</li>
        <li><strong>4</strong>: Demanding. Remote or rough. You need skills and spares.</li>
        <li><strong>5</strong>: Extreme. We do not focus on this level.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="muted">[CHECK this scale before launch]</p>
      <h2>What do you need?</h2>
      <p>A gravel bike or a mountain bike, depending on the route. Each journey says what fits. If you ride an e-bike or ride with kids, the Honest answers tell you if it works.</p>
      <h2>Where to start</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/journeys/tilburg/">Tilburg</a>: two flat loops from the station.</li>
        <li><a href="/bundles/all-along-the-watchtowers/">All Along The Watchtowers</a>: five routes along five towers.</li>
        <li><a href="/destinations/luxembourg/">Luxembourg</a>: a destination guide with three trips.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Want us to ride your region? <a href="/request-a-route/">Request a route</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
